1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,925
Meet Invoice Copilot — a chat-based agent that turns a plain-English request into a real PayPal invoice.

2
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:19,075
Freelancers still lose hours digging through email for client details, rebuilding line items by hand, and chasing payment status across tools.

3
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:29,150
Invoice Copilot fixes that. Chat once, review a confirmation card, then create and send through PayPal — sandbox or live.

4
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:41,250
Here's the path: you describe the job, the agent drafts the invoice, you confirm, PayPal creates and sends it, and the desk shows the link and status.

5
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:52,675
It's built with Next.js, a demo agent or LLM plus the PayPal Agent Toolkit, and human confirmation before every write.

6
00:00:54,600 --> 00:01:01,300
Try demo mode in under a minute — no PayPal keys required. Open the chat and ask for an invoice.

7
00:01:05,402 --> 00:01:11,527
Here is Invoice Copilot on a real PayPal sandbox. Draft, human confirm, and send.

8
00:01:11,838 --> 00:01:17,863
Now the live app. Groq handles tool calling, and PayPal sandbox invoicing is authorized.

9
00:01:17,838 --> 00:01:23,363
I ask Invoice Copilot to bill Acme Sandbox five hundred dollars for logo design.

10
00:01:23,538 --> 00:01:29,038
It creates a real PayPal draft, then asks for human confirmation before sending.

11
00:01:29,338 --> 00:01:35,013
I confirm. PayPal marks the invoice as sent and returns a sandbox payment link.

12
00:01:35,838 --> 00:01:41,513
The invoice desk lists live sandbox invoices. Agentic commerce, end to end.

13
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:53,225
Thanks for watching. Clone the repo, run npm install and npm run dev, then try it with your PayPal sandbox app and a Groq key.
